# FITS is a binary format with an ASCII header, which defeats git's
# text/binary heuristic: it looks for a NUL byte in the first 8 KB, and a
# file with a long enough header has none. So detection came down to header
# length -- wcs_*.fits (header only, no data) read as text outright, and
# bright_star_sloan.fits diffed as 3490 changed lines when two rows were
# removed from it, while the identically-formatted bright_variable_vsx.fits
# was correctly binary because its header is short. Mark them all.
*.fits binary
*.fits.gz binary
*.fits.bz2 binary
